in that behalf, if the Committee thinks it necessary so to do;
(g)
to define the powers and duties of the Advisory Committee;
(h)
to determine the functions and powers, if any, which the Sajjadanashin may exercise in relation to the Durgah;
(i)
to appoint, suspend or dismiss servants of the Durgah Endowment;
(j)
to make such provision for the education and maintenance of the indigent descendants of Khawaja Moin-ud-din Chishti
and their families and the indigent Khadims and their families residing in India as the Committee considers expedient
consistently with the financial position of the Durgah;
(k)
to delegate to the Nazim such powers and functions as the Committee may think fit;
(l)
to do all other such things as may be incidental or conducive to the efficient administration of the Durgah.

